{"ts":"2026-09-01T07:34:13.374Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"b15b98d619eb46723c158c6c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pmc-zgnm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The empty-windows fallback re-fabricates a dated placeholder heading on the library path"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Making an accidentally empty releaseWindows list fall back to absent history closed the silent item loss, but the absent-history path still stamps a version heading with today's date when the caller supplies a version and no date. A library caller that resolves windows with pendingRelease false in a zero-tag repository and forwards package.json's version therefore gets the fabricated heading this pull request exists to remove, dated by the clock. resolveReleaseTagWindows returns a bare array and discards suppressedPendingRelease, so the caller cannot express the suppression the helper performed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["changelog","clock-dependence","library-api","regression"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:34:13.374Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:34:13.374Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An empty windows list plus an untagged version does not fabricate a dated release heading; A real release run supplying version and date still renders its dated heading unchanged; Suppression intent survives resolveReleaseTagWindows, or that helper is guarded against this misuse; A regression test covers the library path and is verified red on revert"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bdaa20a672f22498e420d92394959a0e8b85f6f8a6ad764a91f951f5d3040ce4","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Record the placeholder heading reachable through the library API","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T07:34:26.057Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"b15b98d619eb46723c158c6c","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:34:26.057Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-01T07:34:26.057Z","author":"claude","text":"Reproduced by execution against 6e8ebaa. createChangelog with an empty releaseWindows list and a version, which is what a library caller gets from resolveReleaseTagWindows in a zero-tag repository plus package.json's version:\n\n  { items, releaseWindows: [], version: '2026.7.30' }\n    -> '## 2026.7.30 - 2026-09-01'   FABRICATED, dated by the clock\n  { items, releaseWindows: [], version: '2026.7.30', includeUnreleased: false }\n    -> '## 2026.7.30 - 2026-09-01'   includeUnreleased does not prevent it\n  { items, releaseWindows: [], includeUnreleased: false }\n    -> '## Unreleased'               correct\n  { items, releaseWindows: [], includeUnreleased: false, suppressedPendingRelease: '2026.7.30' }\n    -> '# Changelog' only            deliberate emptiness, correct\n\nThe first two are precisely the defect this pull request exists to remove: a heading asserting a release that never happened, stamped with today's date. The date comes from buildVersionHeading, which stamps new Date() whenever a version is present and no explicit date was supplied. Closing the silent item loss routed the accidental empty list into absent history, and absent history is exactly the path that fabricates.\n\nTwo distinct problems, and both need fixing. First, a versioned heading with no explicit date is still clock-dependent, so the changelog a check run generates today differs from the one written yesterday with no commit in between. Second, resolveReleaseTagWindows returns a bare array and drops suppressedPendingRelease, so a caller who asked the helper to suppress cannot tell the generator that suppression happened; only resolveReleaseTagWindowResolution carries it."}]}],"before_hash":"bdaa20a672f22498e420d92394959a0e8b85f6f8a6ad764a91f951f5d3040ce4","after_hash":"dc9af9ab232c7ad88bcf5741f5b659b2bffc53bb19855cae33304f2462143914","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
