{"ts":"2026-09-01T07:43:06.054Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"05c86a36dc3a7a6b0a623035","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-09-01T07:43:06.054Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Red-on-revert proof (each anchored pattern ran exactly 1 test):\n\n1. Replaced the fixed `buildVersionHeading` body with the prior version branch that used `explicitStamp ?? new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`. `createChangelog does not derive a version heading date from the wall clock` failed 0/1 because simulated 2026-08-01 and 2026-09-01 produced different headings. Restored the fixed hunk; 1/1 passed.\n2. Replaced the fixed `resolveReleaseTagWindows` body with `return resolveReleaseTagWindowResolution(options).windows;`. `resolveReleaseTagWindows carries deliberate empty suppression into createChangelog` failed 0/1 by rendering `## 2026.9.1 - 2026-09-01` and the item instead of title-only deliberate emptiness. Restored the fixed hunk; 1/1 passed.\n3. Replaced the fixed pending-timestamp fallback and conditional heading with `normalizeTimestamp(options.pendingTimestamp ?? new Date().toISOString())` and the always-dated heading. `keeps a pending tag undated when pendingTimestamp is absent` failed 0/1 with `2026.9.9 - 2026-09-01` instead of `2026.9.9`. Restored both hunk lines; 1/1 passed.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-01T07:43:06.054Z"}],"before_hash":"1c81464d96bf5f3867f7a07747fc3f08bd7afb1095cba68bf25aa1c64abaa83e","after_hash":"343b33b19ef93ca7ef0a0d38bb80cbb8e30bf25aa34a5102159d85d7572fe24d","item_hash_version":3}
